  "changes": [
    "Gelato aim now solves the gravity-affected launch trajectory so unobstructed balls reach the reachable finger target at the normal launch speed.",
    "A curved dotted preview follows the solved flight and ends at the target or the first peg contact; both Twin launchers use a shared reachable target.",
    "Initial Gelato launcher jitter is removed, and free flight uses exact gravity integration so actual shots match the displayed trajectory.",
    "Gelato trajectory and Trial rules are revision 2. Previous Gelato Trial times are cleared while campaign wallets, upgrades, Twin ownership and Bakery Trial records remain.",
    "Home menu > Settings > Developer areas bypasses Bakery completion and the Gelato entry fee in developer/debug builds.",
    "An unvisited area starts at tray 1 with zero coins and no upgrades; returning restores its own wallet, upgrades, tray progress and Gelato Twin/Power state across restarts.",
    "Bakery and Gelato use Bronze/Silver/Gold/Diamond strength bands at 6/12/18/24 ordinary-peg HP across trays 1-3/4-6/7-9/10-12.",
    "Gelato uses a top-center downward finger-aimed launcher, gravity, twelve fan layouts and its own economy tuning.",
    "Gelato Twin launchers reset Power once; lost Power nodes remain red and can be rebuilt at higher prices with stronger gains while other upgrades remain.",
    "The export explicitly includes data/gelato_economy.json alongside every current top-level runtime JSON file.",
    "Includes the current canonical sugarfall_save.json migration, confirmed Reset progress, Mabel introduction, countdown feedback and result comparison UI."
  ],
